WEBVTT

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:04.629
Um...

00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:07.131
- What the thorax?
- Are you crazy?

00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:09.759
What? I just wanted
a longer car chase.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.177
It's the best part.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.180
[police radio chatter]

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:15.640
Chief! It's...

00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:17.392
Them.

00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:18.643
[grunts]

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.520
Webs, hit it.

00:00:20.604 --> 00:00:23.272
["Stop, Drop, Roll" plays on radio]

00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:24.899
Get them!

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.693
- [all laughing]
- [engine revs]

00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:34.117
- [officers clamoring]
- [sirens wailing]

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.957
<i>♪ Hooked on hip-hop phonics</i>
<i>Yeah it works for me ♪</i>

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.459
<i>♪ So jump aboard</i>
<i>Yeah, this train is free ♪</i>

00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:45.878
<i>♪ The conductor let me toot my whistle ♪</i>

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.715
<i>♪ The instructor</i>
<i>Of the funky uncle fizzle ♪</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:50.800
<i>♪ We be dancing on a lake</i>
<i>When it ain't froze over ♪</i>

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.094
<i>♪ We be walking on water</i>
<i>While you're sinking your rover ♪</i>

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:55.304
<i>♪ If you step any close</i>
<i>You'll be eatin' some teeth ♪</i>

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.808
[cackling]

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:02.979
I'm gonna put you guys away for so long,
your fleas will have fleas!

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.106
[Chief grunts]

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.441
[all gasp]

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:09.444
Chief! You want some cake?

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:12.238
- You seem a little hangry.
- [all laughing]

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.449
Get that thing out of my face before I...

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:16.033
- Excuse me, Chief.
- What?

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.462
[siren wailing continues]

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:31.966
You're mine.

00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:34.552
[engine revs]

00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:38.765
<i>Hermano!</i>

00:01:42.269 --> 00:01:43.644
[tires squealing]

00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:46.522
[Wolf] Whoo!

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.816
[all screaming]

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:11.339
Yeah. We may be bad,
but we're so good at it.

00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:13.049
[all laughing]

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:20.223
No, no, no, no, no!

00:02:20.307 --> 00:02:22.725
No, no! Keep runnin', Wolf.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.770
One of these days
your luck is gonna run out.

00:02:48.252 --> 00:02:49.669
[elevator bell dings]

00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.885
All right, Piranha. You're up.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.306
[vocalizing]

00:03:02.391 --> 00:03:03.891
<i>Happy birth...</i>

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:05.810
- [gasps]
- Seriously?

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:07.770
Snake, come on.
At least make a toast.

00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:09.564
- Toast.
- Come on.

00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:11.315
- Okay, all right, a toast.
- Yeah!

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.483
Fine.

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.527
I've made a lot of enemies in my time.

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:16.070
I mean, a lot!

00:03:16.154 --> 00:03:18.197
But out of all the people in the world,

00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:21.158
I hate you guys the least.

00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:22.827
That was actually
kind of beautiful.

00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:23.911
You a poet, man.

00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:28.165
To Mr. Snake
and his strange dislike of birthdays.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.543
[all cheering]

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:33.254
Everyone say, "Robbery!"

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:35.131
[all] Robbery!

00:03:36.091 --> 00:03:38.175
Look at those dimples.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.510
Happy birthday, buddy.

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.178
Okay. Now, dig in, fellas.

00:03:41.263 --> 00:03:42.471
Yes! [laughs]

00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:44.056
- No, no, no!
- Piranha!

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:46.767
- [Wolf] Don't do that.
- [Tarantula] That was so gross.

00:03:46.852 --> 00:03:48.352
[Shark] That was my lunch.

00:03:48.437 --> 00:03:50.521
- [Piranha] You snooze, you lose.
- [Tarantula laughing]

00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:51.856
[Wolf] You like that.

00:03:53.275 --> 00:03:54.275
Nice.

00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:57.236
- Ooh! Wow!
- [Snake gasps]

00:03:57.321 --> 00:03:59.030
I forgot we had those Push Pops.

00:03:59.114 --> 00:04:01.782
Man, my tummy is rumblin'
like a kraken right now.

00:04:01.867 --> 00:04:03.576
Yeah. Want it?

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.828
You know he's not
gonna give it to you.

00:04:05.913 --> 00:04:10.207
No. I believe that, deep down,
Snake is a kind and generous soul.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.335
Why?

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:14.503
Here. Take it.

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:17.006
Oh, yeah! Pop me, please.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.259
[gasps, sighs]

00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:22.136
- [laughs] Sucker.
- Come on, man!

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.138
Now you're gonna make me
get all aggressive.

00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:28.684
- Animals.
- Spit it out! Spit it out!

00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:29.852
[Snake] Never!

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.646
Let's see
what they're sayin' about us today.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.066
<i>What up? It's Tiffany Fluffit,</i>
<i>Channel 6 Action News.</i>

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.359
<i>The Bad Guys have struck again...</i>

00:04:36.443 --> 00:04:38.903
- Guys, stop it. We're on TV.
<i>- ...with their most brazen heist yet,</i>

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:43.950
<i>proving once more that they are</i>
<i>the most diabolical criminals of our time.</i>

00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:45.910
"Diabolical." That's new.

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:47.870
Know what it sounds like? A cologne.

00:04:47.955 --> 00:04:48.871
"Diabolical."

00:04:48.956 --> 00:04:50.831
<i>To address this heinous crime spree</i>

00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:53.960
<i>is the newly elected governor,</i>
<i>Diane Foxington.</i>

00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:55.461
- Governor?
- [Diane] Okay, yeah.

00:04:55.545 --> 00:04:56.837
<i>I hear you. I hear you.</i>

00:04:56.922 --> 00:04:58.047
<i>Listen, listen.</i>

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.800
<i>We all know</i>
<i>how dastardly the Bad Guys are.</i>

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:02.093
You bet we are.

00:05:02.177 --> 00:05:05.221
<i>But more than anything...</i>
[chuckles]

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.555
<i>...I feel sorry for them.</i>

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:07.682
What?

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.895
<i>These so-called "Bad Guys"</i>
<i>are really just second-rate has-beens.</i>

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:17.274
<i>Behind their amateurish antics</i>
<i>and, frankly, unoriginal capers...</i>

00:05:17.359 --> 00:05:19.235
<i>I mean, really? Another bank?</i>

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.487
<i>...is nothing but a deep well of anger.</i>

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:22.989
I ain't angry! You're angry!

00:05:23.073 --> 00:05:24.699
<i>- Denial.</i>
- Not true.

00:05:24.783 --> 00:05:25.866
<i>And self-loathing.</i>

00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:28.202
The only one I self-loathe is you.

00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:33.416
<i>And those are holes that no amount of cash</i>
<i>or priceless art can ever fill.</i>

00:05:35.877 --> 00:05:37.920
What's on the Food Network?

00:05:38.005 --> 00:05:40.923
<i>- Can we just forget about the Bad Guys...</i>
- Who is she to judge us?

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:43.217
<i>- ...and focus on more positive things?</i>
- [growls]

00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:46.929
<i>And what could be more positive</i>
<i>than the Annual Good Samaritan Awards,</i>

00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:48.931
<i>where tomorrow night I will present</i>

00:05:49.016 --> 00:05:52.810
<i>the Golden Dolphin</i>
<i>to this year's goodest citizen.</i>

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.105
- I can't believe I voted for her.
- You voted for her?

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.940
[Tarantula]
What? She's good on climate change.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:02.862
Wait. What's going on?
You've got that twinkle in your eye.

00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:08.492
Guys, who's up for another job?

00:06:08.577 --> 00:06:09.744
A big one.

00:06:10.704 --> 00:06:11.704
[all gasp]

00:06:12.456 --> 00:06:14.040
The Golden Dolphin.

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:15.124
Seriously?

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.168
Oh! I thought I was
the crazy one.

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:19.754
That job has broken every criminal
who's tried it.

00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:22.465
<i>The Bucharest Bandits. Lucky Jim.</i>

00:06:22.549 --> 00:06:23.799
<i>The Crimson Paw.</i>

00:06:23.884 --> 00:06:26.135
Actually, the Crimson Paw
was never arrested.

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.471
Yeah, but he never stole anything again.

00:06:28.555 --> 00:06:31.599
Snake, what better way
to wipe that smirk off

00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:33.100
the governor's fuzzy face,

00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:36.395
than stealin' the Golden Dolphin
from right under her whiskers?

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.106
This is the holy grail of thievery.

00:06:39.191 --> 00:06:40.357
If we pull this off,

00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:43.486
we'll cement our legacy
as the greatest criminals of all time.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:45.112
Whoa, whoa, buddy.

00:06:45.197 --> 00:06:47.823
I thought we weren't supposed to
make things personal.

00:06:47.908 --> 00:06:49.909
Besides, we've got
a good thing goin' here.

00:06:49.993 --> 00:06:53.537
Friends, freedom,
and just look at this loot!

